      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pine%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The White Pine mine operated by the Copper Range Company from 1955 to 1995.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Pine%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits within Carp Lake Township, which began as a copper mining hub in 1858 near the Carp Lake Copper Mine.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carplaketwp.org/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Finnish immigrants later added logging and farming, turning the area into a rural community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.carplaketwp.org/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Nonesuch Mine, once a bustling copper mine, became a ghost town after closing.",
